 "bloques": [
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Talk about the family",
   "texto": [
    "The words of kinship usually carry article: far (a father), mor (a mother), et barn (a child / creature). In Bokmål it can also be used in many words feminine: in søster.",
    "In Norwegian, the possessive may go after a defined noun: broren min means «My brother»; literally, «My brother.». The end - it's equivalent here to «the».",
    "Barn has the same shape in singular and plural: et barn, flere barn. For people they are used han («He») and hun («her.»)."
   ]
  },
